cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "vibe-coding-blindspot-checker"
abstract: >-
  An agent skill that reads a person's own coding-agent sessions and finds the
  decisions the agent made that the person never made, still in the code, ordered
  by The Command Scale v1.0. It carries the scale's normative text and an
  implementation that passes its conformance cases.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/yabeiz/vibe-coding-blindspot-checker"
authors:
  - name: "Yabei Z."
    website: "https://github.com/yabeiz"
keywords:
  - vibe coding
  - coding agents
  - agent skills
  - code review
  - The Command Scale
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Measuring what a person can get an AI to build"
  abstract: >-
    A six-level scale of the ability to use what a machine already knows — its
    derivation, its instrument, and what building it taught us.
  authors:
    - name: "Mentor by farsurf"
      website: "https://mentor.farsurf.com"
  year: 2026
  notes: >-
    White paper, version 1.0, pre-publication draft. The normative text is
    Appendix B together with Appendix A and sections 4, 5 and 9 of the paper.
    Levels: L1 Note, L2 Verse, L3 Canon, L4 Chronicle, L5 Saga, L6 Myth.
    Licensed CC BY 4.0.
  url: "https://github.com/farsurf/command-scale/blob/main/spec/the-command-scale-v1.0.md"
